What are Grouting Materials?
Grouting materials are flowable plastic substances designed to fill gaps, voids, or cracks in structures. These materials must demonstrate negligible shrinkage to ensure complete filling and remain stable over time without cracking, delamination, or crumbling. Injection grouting is a common application method, involving the pressurized placement of material into cracks, voids, or honeycombs in concrete or masonry structures to repair damage, strengthen elements, or provide waterproofing.

